{"document":1,"title":"user in #09d032c9:answer_b10dce5e: I'm looking for some advice on the best way to org...","updated_at":"2023-05-27T06:12:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"The eternal struggle of keeping tech accessories organized while traveling! I'm happy to help you with that. Here are some tips to keep your portable power bank, wireless charging pad, and other tech accessories tidy and easily accessible while on the go: 1. **Travel case or pouch**: Invest in a dedicated travel case or pouch specifically designed for tech accessories. These cases usually have multiple compartments, pockets, and dividers to keep your items organized and protected. 2. **Cable organizers**: Use cable organizers or cord wraps to manage your cables and prevent tangles. You can also use small ziplock bags or travel-sized cable organizers to keep your cables tidy. 3. **Power bank pouch**: Consider a separate pouch or sleeve for your portable power bank to protect it from scratches and damage. 4. **Wireless charging pad case**: If your wireless charging pad doesn't come with a built-in case, look for a protective sleeve or pouch to store it in. 5. **Ziplock bags**: Use small ziplock bags to store small items like earbuds, adapters, or extra batteries. Label each bag so you can easily find what you need. 6. **Travel wallet or passport holder**: If you have a travel wallet or passport holder, consider storing your tech accessories in a dedicated pocket or compartment. 7. **Pack by category**: Organize your tech accessories by category, such as charging cables, adapters, power banks, and wireless charging pads. This makes it easier to find what you need quickly. 8. **Keep frequently used items accessible**: Store your most frequently used items, like your phone and portable power bank, in easy-to-reach pockets or compartments. 9. **Consider a tech accessory roll**: If you have a lot of small items, consider a tech accessory roll, which can be rolled up and secured with Velcro or a strap. 10. **Label and color-code**: Label each item or category with its contents, and consider color-coding your cables or accessories to make them easier to identify.","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"09d032c9:answer_b10dce5e\"}"}
