{"document":1,"title":"user in #18dcd5a5:answer_sharegpt_hn3IS1q_0: create a D&D one shot for level 8 PCs. Include sta...","updated_at":"2023-05-29T22:34:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"create a D&D one shot for level 8 PCs. Include stat blocks for the enemies and loot if they succeed. the final battle should include a suprise twist. also, there should be cool layer actions. If there are any traps, describe in detail. Also, describe in detail all aspects of the one-shot to help a GM run the one shot smoothly\n\"The Lost Temple of the Djinn\" Ages ago, a powerful Djinn named Zoltar ruled over a vast temple filled with treasures and magical artifacts. Zoltar was a just ruler and the temple flourished under his rule. But as time passed, Zoltar disappeared and the temple was lost to the sands of time. Now, a wealthy collector has hired the party to retrieve an artifact from the lost temple. The collector has located the temple and believes the artifact to be located within its walls, but he doesn't have the power to retrieve it himself. Upon arriving at the temple, the party must navigate through a series of traps and puzzles to reach the artifact. The temple is filled with mummies, undead warriors, and constructs guarding its treasures. Here are the stat blocks for the enemies the party will face: * Mummies (4): + Armor Class: 11 + Hit Points: 45 (6d8 + 18) + Speed: 20 ft. + Damage Immunity: Poison, Psychicical + Condition Immunity: Charmed, Exhaustion, Frightened, Paralyzed, Petrified, Poisoned + Traits: - Curse of the Pharaohs. A creature that touches the mummy or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 ft. of it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or be cursed. The cursed target can't regain hit points, and its hit point maximum is reduced by 10 (3d6) for 24 hours. The curse lasts until removed by a remove curse spell or similar magic. - Mummy Rot. A creature hit by a mummy's Slam attack must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or be affected by the Mummy Rot disease. The disease's effects are detailed in appendix A of the Monster Manuel. * Construct Guardians (2): + Armor Class: 17 (natural armor) + Hit Points: 110 (13d10 + 30) + Speed: 30 ft. + Damage Immunity: Poison, Psychicical + Condition Immunity: Charmed, Exhaustion, Frightened, Paralyzed, Petrified, Poisoned + Traits: - Immutable Form. The construct is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form. - Magic Resistance. The construct has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects. - Magic Weapons.","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"18dcd5a5:answer_sharegpt_hn3IS1q_0\"}"}
